# ── Keep the relay's build context to what the relay actually compiles ───────
# The relay image builds `-p farder-relay`, which needs Cargo.{toml,lock}, the
# workspace crates, and the root package's own `tests/` + `src/` (the workspace
# root is itself a package, so removing those breaks `cargo build`).
#
# Everything below is context that only ever invalidates the COPY layer. It
# cost a full ~20-minute Rust rebuild after a website copy edit, which is how it
# was noticed: `compose up --build` re-ran the whole compile because a paragraph
# on the landing page changed.
website/
docs/
client/
nvenc-probe/
scripts/
*.md
